    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332">

                <pb facs="0322" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112A European War, 1939/4094:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-11-25T20:00:00-05:00">November 25, 1941—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 26—1:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>581. Since there have been several instances of imports into Colombia on Dutch
                    ships from Brazil and Argentina by firms on Proclaimed List the Department might
                    care to enlist the cooperation of the Netherlands to instruct their shipping
                    companies not to accept cargo for proclaimed firms.<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d332-f1"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Braden</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d332-f1" n="42" xml:id="d332-f1-content">
                <p>In Department’s telegram No. 489, December 11, 8 p.m., the Ambassador In Colombia
                    was informed that the matter had been discussed with representatives of the
                    Netherlands Legation and that they had agreed to have instructions sent out to
                    remedy the situation (740.00112A European War, 1939/4094).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
